  "user_request_original": "Design a 24-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 multilayer filter on fused silica substrate at 0 degree incidence with unpolarized light. Layer sequence: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2... (24 total layers, starting with Ta2O5). Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 560 nm geometric mean wavelength (Ta2O5: 560/(4*n_Ta2O5), SiO2: 560/(4*n_SiO2)), then optimize all 24 thicknesses with bounds 20-350 nm. Simulation wavelength grid: 601 points from 350 nm to 1100 nm ensuring coverage of 355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, and 1030-1080 nm bands. Optimize for minimum mean transmittance in 355-365 nm and 1030-1080 nm bands, minimum transmittance at 355 nm, and maximum mean transmittance in 420-700 nm band. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with 1000 iterations maximum. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 8 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs (16 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize 16 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 coating layers on fused silica under normal-incidence unpolarized illumination to suppress transmittance in 355 nm, 355–365 nm, and 1030–1080 nm spectral bands while maximizing transmittance in 420–700 nm, constraining all layer thicknesses to 20–350 nm bounds.",
